ctlq_20260909 -- KILL TABLE for `pcc2c040ctlq' (follow-up under #512 pcc2c040kill)
Opus 5 measuring seat, scratch clone /tmp/gxopusctlq (cp -a of build/), 2026-09-09..10.

THE FINDING, MEASURED:  `genctl ctlq' -- the ACCEPT row the de-escalation clause owes for the
C040 predicate -- was keyed on the PRE-FIX fatal() text, which #512 retired.  It was green under
the shipped fix and under every post-fix mutant, so it was discharged BY EXISTING.  A guard
WIDENING onto the benign bit it drives SWEPT THE 16-ROW DETECTOR CLEAN.

INSTRUMENTS (frozen copies; one instrument per comparison)
  SHIPPED   md5 a36b6a47e1001cc59c3ab02978d5ffda   = regress/pcc2_c040_probe.py at HEAD e73623a
  REPAIRED  md5 cbe1945cffe7f3441cc93d5489bdc692   = ./pcc2_c040_probe.REPAIRED.py

BASELINE IDENTITY (named, per the clone recipe)
  clone src/devices/dev_pcc2.c  cmp  GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_pcc2.c   ->  IDENTICAL
  (git status: dev_pcc2.c clean against HEAD; the +21 comment hunk the 2026-09-09 review
   warned about was committed in 816e153, so working tree == HEAD == the measured source)
  baseline rebuilt IN THE CLONE before mutant 1; [ gxemul -nt dev_pcc2.c ] OK on every build.

THE MUTANT
  M_widen   src/devices/dev_pcc2.c, reassert_interrupts(), the C040 test -- ONE line:

      -	if (d->pcctwo_reg[PCCTWO_GENCTL] & PCC2_C040) {
      +	if (d->pcctwo_reg[PCCTWO_GENCTL] & (PCC2_C040 | 0x10)) {

  0x10 is the probe's own BENIGN value.  It is an UNNAMED GENCTL bit -- mvme_pcctworeg.h names
  only DR0 0x80, C040 0x04, MIEN 0x02, FAST 0x01 -- which is exactly why a benign write of it is
  legal and why `genctl ctl' / `genctl ctlq' drive it.  This is the canonical accept-side GROWTH
  mutant: guard-only, because the latch operand `(1u << PCC2_W_C040)' is a compile-time constant
  the guard cannot feed, and the carrier's discriminator selects guard-only at such a site.

  NON-EQUIVALENCE IS MEASURED, not argued: under M_widen the repaired `genctl ctlq' reads `yes',
  i.e. the benign 0x10 write DID reach the arm and DID emit the announce.  A mutant that swept a
  table without being observable anywhere would be an equivalent mutant, not an escape.

