=================================================================================================

  mutant          recorded (its own denominator)                   now, REPAIRED @ 16 rows
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  M_return         9/10  killtable_20260908/M_return.raw            14/16  KILL PRESERVED
                   red: c040 noassert                               red: c040 noassert
                                                                       + c040 noassert2
  M_latchinside   10/10  killtable_20260908/M_latchinside.raw       15/16  KILL PRESERVED
                   *** ESCAPED at 10 rows ***                       red: c040 noassert2
                   10/11  killtable_20260908/M_latchinside2.raw
                   red: c040 noassert2
  M_d1_noassert    9/10  killtable_20260908/M_d1_noassert.raw       14/16  KILL PRESERVED
                   red: c040 noassert                               red: c040 noassert
                                                                       + c040 noassert2

  READ THE ARITHMETIC, NOT THE FRACTION.  9/10 -> 14/16 is not a weakened kill: 10 rows minus
  9 ok = ONE red; 16 rows minus 14 ok = TWO red.  The extra red is `c040 noassert2', a row that
  did not exist when the 10-row table ran (it was added in table 3).  M_return and M_d1_noassert
  null the repair on EVERY encounter, so they redden both encounter rows; M_latchinside nulls it
  only from the second encounter on, so it reddens exactly one.  Each mutant reddens the rows its
  own mechanism predicts.

  `genctl ctlq' is GREEN on all three spot-check mutants and on BASE.  The repair adds no false
  red; it reddens under exactly one thing, which is the widening it exists to catch.

  This also discharges hygiene note 2 of the 2026-09-09 review -- "no mutant has been scored
  against the shipped 16-row instrument".  Four now have been.

